    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nindentscope\n\n### Description\n\nHi again @echasnovski,\r\n\r\nObviously I can workaround that with autocommands and `b:miniindentscope_disable` but I think it would be nice to have an option to disable the plugin for certain filetypes (e.g. `fzf`, `NvimTree`, etc) and buftypes (e.g. `nofile`, `terminal`).\r\n\r\nIndent-blankline, for example, supports exclusions with both `filetype_exclude` and `buftype_exclude`",
